1
00:00:06,548 --> 00:00:08,175
FIVE DAYS AGO

2
00:00:10,928 --> 00:00:14,973
Father, I can sense Demons
in this town as well.

3
00:00:15,474 --> 00:00:18,769
Yes... I can smell them.

4
00:00:20,354 --> 00:00:21,230
Keisuke, over here!

5
00:00:21,355 --> 00:00:22,689
Is it a Demon, Father?!

6
00:00:23,273 --> 00:00:24,358
I've located a lady!

7
00:00:26,193 --> 00:00:27,110
Father!!

8
00:00:27,277 --> 00:00:29,446
Keisuke, go somewhere
for a little bit!

9
00:00:29,613 --> 00:00:32,199
No, we need to
track down the Demons!

10
00:00:32,449 --> 00:00:34,409
Please, Keisuke, please!

11
00:00:34,535 --> 00:00:35,494
Eek! You're scaring me!

12
00:00:35,619 --> 00:00:36,703
N-No!

13
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:45,879
Hey Missy,
let's have some fun!

14
00:00:47,297 --> 00:00:48,131
We need to help her!

15
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:49,174
Wait!

16
00:00:49,341 --> 00:00:51,635
We could y'know,
do this... or that...

17
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:53,595
Let's have fun!
Let's have fun!

18
00:00:53,637 --> 00:00:54,471
What? A human?

19
00:00:55,681 --> 00:00:56,515
Huh?

20
00:00:56,682 --> 00:00:58,267
What do you want?

21
00:01:07,818 --> 00:01:08,652
Let's hide!

22
00:01:12,990 --> 00:01:14,074
Let's follow him, Keisuke!

23
00:01:14,116 --> 00:01:14,950
All right!

24
00:01:19,663 --> 00:01:20,497
There he is.

25
00:01:32,092 --> 00:01:34,136
All right,
let's check out that room.

26
00:01:34,219 --> 00:01:35,053
All right!

27
00:01:37,514 --> 00:01:38,348
Wait, Keisuke!

28
00:01:38,557 --> 00:01:39,391
Huh?

29
00:01:43,395 --> 00:01:44,730
D-Demons?

30
00:01:44,771 --> 00:01:46,690
But I don't sense any bloodlust
coming from them.

31
00:01:47,024 --> 00:01:49,026
That's not all...

32
00:01:49,151 --> 00:01:51,278
It's almost as if
their life force is gone,

33
00:01:51,403 --> 00:01:53,280
like they're just empty shells.

34
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:56,825
Also... look at how many there are.

35
00:01:57,284 --> 00:01:58,910
So, did that boy do this
all by himself?

36
00:01:59,119 --> 00:02:02,331
If that's the case...
What's his endgame?

37
00:02:02,956 --> 00:02:03,790
Watch out!

38
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:06,335
Damn it!

39
00:02:06,877 --> 00:02:07,711
Father!

40
00:02:12,507 --> 00:02:14,301
I knew you were following me.

41
00:02:14,593 --> 00:02:15,427
<i>Damn it!</i>

42
00:02:15,510 --> 00:02:17,387
<i>I couldn't sense him at all!</i>

43
00:02:17,804 --> 00:02:20,807
Hikari, could these be...?

44
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:22,934
Yeah. Seems like it.

45
00:02:23,352 --> 00:02:25,604
The descendants of
the Goshikidori Family.

46
00:02:25,771 --> 00:02:27,522
What an unexpected turn of events...

47
00:02:27,773 --> 00:02:28,732
How do you know?!

48
00:02:29,066 --> 00:02:31,026
Heard it from the higher-ups.

49
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:34,404
Sounds like they have
some questions for you.

50
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:36,073
<i>They can understand me?</i>

51
00:02:36,782 --> 00:02:38,367
Are you both Demons?

52
00:02:38,784 --> 00:02:39,660
Demons?

53
00:02:40,994 --> 00:02:41,995
No.

54
00:02:42,663 --> 00:02:44,206
We're Devils.

55
00:02:44,581 --> 00:02:46,166
The chosen ones.

56
00:02:46,875 --> 00:02:48,210
D-Devils?!

57
00:02:48,835 --> 00:02:52,297
#31, #56, Seize him!

58
00:03:09,314 --> 00:03:10,732
Not bad.

59
00:03:11,066 --> 00:03:12,109
I guess...

60
00:03:15,112 --> 00:03:16,947
I'll entertain you a bit.

61
00:03:30,419 --> 00:03:32,754
Hey, come on...
We're not supposed to kill them.

62
00:03:32,921 --> 00:03:34,798
Oh. My bad.

63
00:03:38,385 --> 00:03:40,387
<i>I can take on the Demons...</i>

64
00:03:40,595 --> 00:03:43,640
<i>But I don't think I can win
against those Devils...</i>

65
00:03:44,057 --> 00:03:45,767
Well, what are you gonna do?

66
00:03:46,184 --> 00:03:50,480
R-Run... Keisuke...

67
00:03:53,066 --> 00:03:53,942
Get him!

68
00:03:54,443 --> 00:03:57,821
<i>I promise
I'll come back for you, Father.</i>

69
00:03:57,946 --> 00:03:59,739
<i>Please hold on!</i>

70
00:04:03,869 --> 00:04:06,455
<i>Damn it!
How am I going to rescue him?!</i>

71
00:04:06,997 --> 00:04:10,041
I can't do this on my own.
I need help.

72
00:04:11,585 --> 00:04:12,419
<i>Keisuke...</i>

73
00:04:12,878 --> 00:04:15,672
<i>You actually have
an older half-brother.</i>

74
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:17,716
<i>His name is Keiji.</i>

75
00:04:18,216 --> 00:04:20,677
<i>The day may come when
you'll fight side-by-side.</i>

76
00:04:22,012 --> 00:04:23,764
<i>That's right!
I have an older brother</i>!

77
00:04:24,556 --> 00:04:27,100
<i>But how do I find him?</i>

78
00:04:29,311 --> 00:04:31,229
Hey, look at this chicken!

79
00:04:32,147 --> 00:04:33,106
It's crazy...

80
00:04:33,231 --> 00:04:34,983
He blew that
Demon's head right off!

81
00:04:35,108 --> 00:04:37,068
What the hell?
He's amazing!

82
00:04:37,194 --> 00:04:39,446
Seems like he was spotted
in Midorino City yesterday.

83
00:04:39,571 --> 00:04:40,405
<i>That's gotta be...!</i>

84
00:04:44,451 --> 00:04:47,162
Midorino City is
three mountains away.

85
00:04:50,665 --> 00:04:52,918
Him? I saw him by the station.

86
00:04:53,168 --> 00:04:55,003
Oh. that man whore.

87
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:57,255
We just had a group date
with him the other day!

88
00:04:57,380 --> 00:04:59,466
What a waste of time, huh?

89
00:05:06,515 --> 00:05:09,768
I finally found you.

90
00:05:10,644 --> 00:05:12,771
Big Brother...

91
00:06:56,916 --> 00:06:59,878
EPISODE 8
NOT ALL FEATHERS HOLD A SONG

92
00:07:00,837 --> 00:07:05,550
309, 310, 311...

93
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:09,763
312, 313, 314...

94
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:13,350
315, 316...

95
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:13,767
DUTY

96
00:07:13,558 --> 00:07:16,311
- <i>Even if I left...
- 317, 318, 319...</i>

97
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:18,396
<i>it wouldn't change anything.</i>

98
00:07:18,647 --> 00:07:19,481
320...

99
00:07:20,023 --> 00:07:22,984
<i>Eat up so you can grow up
big and strong!</i>

100
00:07:23,610 --> 00:07:25,028
323...32—!

101
00:07:25,153 --> 00:07:27,614
Pops... I miss you so much.

102
00:07:34,579 --> 00:07:36,039
Oh, you're awake!

103
00:07:36,915 --> 00:07:37,874
I'm so glad!

104
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:39,876
You're okay now.

105
00:07:43,588 --> 00:07:47,133
You should stay still,
your wounds aren't completely healed yet.

106
00:07:48,218 --> 00:07:51,471
<i>Th-That's right. I passed out.</i>

107
00:07:51,846 --> 00:07:56,226
Y-Y-You were the one who
nursed me back to health?!

108
00:07:56,476 --> 00:07:59,521
I didn't do much,
I just stayed by your side.

109
00:07:59,646 --> 00:08:01,731
S-S-Stayed by my side?!

110
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:04,567
Uh, th-thank you so much!

111
00:08:04,943 --> 00:08:06,444
I-I 'm very grateful!

112
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:07,696
Th-Thank you so much!

113
00:08:07,862 --> 00:08:09,239
<i>Is this kid...</i>

114
00:08:09,406 --> 00:08:11,199
<i>Not used to talking to women?</i>

115
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:13,743
<i>Well then...</i>

116
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:15,870
- Th-Thank you so much!
- Um, uh...

117
00:08:15,995 --> 00:08:19,124
No, no, no!
You should rest more!

118
00:08:19,249 --> 00:08:20,709
I-I'm all right!

119
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,752
I-I'm totally feeling better!

120
00:08:22,877 --> 00:08:26,256
But you really should stay
still and rest more.

121
00:08:26,381 --> 00:08:27,757
Might be for the best...

122
00:08:28,591 --> 00:08:30,260
<i>What a funny guy!</i>

123
00:08:32,637 --> 00:08:34,514
B-Big Brother!

124
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:37,475
Damn it,
quit messing around.

125
00:08:38,017 --> 00:08:40,895
First, you call me Big Brother...
Then you pass out for two days...

126
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:43,982
And now that you're awake,
you're horny?

127
00:08:44,649 --> 00:08:46,234
You've got it all wrong, Keiji!

128
00:08:46,359 --> 00:08:47,235
I was just...

129
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:49,612
I think you have me mixed up
with someone else.

130
00:08:49,821 --> 00:08:51,489
I don't have a younger brother.

131
00:08:51,698 --> 00:08:53,366
So, who the hell are you?!

132
00:08:55,952 --> 00:09:00,957
M-My name is Keisuke.
I'm your younger half-brother.

133
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:04,544
Younger...

134
00:09:04,669 --> 00:09:05,920
...half-brother?!

135
00:09:06,463 --> 00:09:09,799
You better not be lying?
Do you have any proof?

136
00:09:10,175 --> 00:09:13,470
We met once as kids.

137
00:09:17,515 --> 00:09:18,892
<i>He's...!</i>

138
00:09:24,606 --> 00:09:25,690
<i>Wait!</i>

139
00:09:25,815 --> 00:09:26,983
<i>This is for you, Sari.</i>

140
00:09:27,108 --> 00:09:30,153
<i>Oh! You made this for me?</i>

141
00:09:31,029 --> 00:09:32,530
<i>Well, does it look good on me?</i>

142
00:09:32,906 --> 00:09:35,784
<i>Oh, uh... Yeah, not bad.</i>

143
00:09:37,202 --> 00:09:38,620
<i>Thank you, dear.</i>

144
00:09:38,995 --> 00:09:40,789
<i>Guess who?!</i>

145
00:09:40,914 --> 00:09:42,248
<i>I wonder who it could be?</i>

146
00:09:42,373 --> 00:09:43,458
<i>I don't know!</i>

147
00:09:44,459 --> 00:09:46,669
<i>You sure got her!
Good job, Keiji!</i>

148
00:09:46,795 --> 00:09:50,381
<i>Aw Dad!
You just gave me away!</i>

149
00:09:51,591 --> 00:09:53,093
<i>You're the worst!</i>

150
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:56,262
<i>I love you so much, Dad!</i>

151
00:09:57,305 --> 00:09:59,349
<i>I'm going for a walk, Mom!</i>

152
00:09:59,599 --> 00:10:01,518
<i>Watch out for stray cats!</i>

153
00:10:03,561 --> 00:10:04,854
<i>Go ahead, hop on my back!</i>

154
00:10:05,814 --> 00:10:07,107
<i>That's Dad's voice!</i>

155
00:10:07,690 --> 00:10:08,525
<i>Dad...!</i>

156
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,820
<i>Yay! Higher! Higher!</i>

157
00:10:12,946 --> 00:10:14,072
<i>D-Dad?!</i>

158
00:10:19,035 --> 00:10:20,078
<i>Who's that?</i>

159
00:10:20,495 --> 00:10:21,830
<i>What's he doing with Dad?!</i>

160
00:10:22,163 --> 00:10:23,123
<i>Hey there...</i>

161
00:10:23,915 --> 00:10:25,917
<i>Are you from the neighborhood?</i>

162
00:10:26,167 --> 00:10:28,253
<i>Do you wanna play?</i>

163
00:10:35,343 --> 00:10:38,388
You're that brat from that day...!

164
00:10:38,930 --> 00:10:43,309
I didn't learn until much later
that we were related.

165
00:10:44,185 --> 00:10:47,230
Brother, I came here
because I need to ask you a favor.

166
00:10:48,148 --> 00:10:50,316
Father is being held hostage
by some Demons.

167
00:10:50,984 --> 00:10:52,652
Will you help me save him?

168
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:57,365
I know that you've been
on a journey battling Demons.

169
00:10:57,740 --> 00:10:58,867
Father told me.

170
00:10:59,951 --> 00:11:01,619
<i>How does he know?!</i>

171
00:11:02,036 --> 00:11:05,248
Our enemies are powerful.
I need your help, Brother.

172
00:11:06,916 --> 00:11:09,210
I know this request may sound callous...

173
00:11:09,586 --> 00:11:12,505
But I need to save Father,
no matter what.

174
00:11:12,839 --> 00:11:14,090
Please, Brother!

175
00:11:16,634 --> 00:11:17,468
I refuse.

176
00:11:19,554 --> 00:11:20,597
W-Why?

177
00:11:20,847 --> 00:11:22,348
He's your real father, isn't he?

178
00:11:22,557 --> 00:11:25,518
I've got nothing to do with that man.

179
00:11:25,977 --> 00:11:26,895
<i>Dad!</i>

180
00:11:28,438 --> 00:11:29,480
<i>Dad!</i>

181
00:11:30,857 --> 00:11:32,692
<i>Dad! Don't leave!</i>

182
00:11:33,902 --> 00:11:34,986
<i>Dear...</i>

183
00:11:35,904 --> 00:11:37,822
<i>Dad!</i>

184
00:11:38,865 --> 00:11:41,242
<i>Dad!</i>

185
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:47,457
Not long after that,
my mother got sick from the heartbreak.

186
00:11:47,999 --> 00:11:49,500
<i>Mom, are you feeling better?</i>

187
00:11:50,001 --> 00:11:52,503
<i>Yes, I'll be better any day now.</i>

188
00:11:53,588 --> 00:11:55,840
But then, one morning...

189
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:00,929
My mother was dead.

190
00:12:02,555 --> 00:12:05,391
Leaving behind
her newborn child, Sarah.

191
00:12:06,226 --> 00:12:11,564
My mother had protected
the last egg she had with my father.

192
00:12:11,773 --> 00:12:14,776
She whittled away her life
incubating it.

193
00:12:17,528 --> 00:12:19,072
<i>Why, Mom?</i>

194
00:12:19,614 --> 00:12:21,866
<i>Why would you do this
for that bastard's child?!</i>

195
00:12:22,617 --> 00:12:25,453
<i>Mom!</i>

196
00:12:26,746 --> 00:12:31,334
I don't care that
he had another family.

197
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:35,630
But, my mother died
of a broken heart.

198
00:12:36,089 --> 00:12:37,840
I'll never forgive him for that.

199
00:12:38,591 --> 00:12:42,637
He killed my mother.
And I'll never forgive him.

200
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:46,556
I'm sorry you went through all of that.

201
00:12:46,557 --> 00:12:48,600
But I don't see how
that's directly Father's fault.

202
00:12:48,601 --> 00:12:49,435
What did you say?

203
00:12:49,978 --> 00:12:51,854
How would you know?

204
00:12:52,188 --> 00:12:57,485
How could the kid lovingly raised
by that piece of crap know anything?

205
00:12:58,152 --> 00:13:00,113
"Piece of crap"?

206
00:13:00,363 --> 00:13:02,824
If you don't like the word "crap..."
"garbage" works too.

207
00:13:02,949 --> 00:13:05,285
You're free to think
what you want, Brother.

208
00:13:05,618 --> 00:13:09,247
But to me, he's the father
and mentor that I respect.

209
00:13:09,455 --> 00:13:11,666
I won't tolerate any more slander.

210
00:13:11,916 --> 00:13:13,918
Not even from you, Brother.

211
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:16,546
Let's calm down a little, shall we?

212
00:13:16,671 --> 00:13:17,797
Hey, Keiji!

213
00:13:21,175 --> 00:13:24,470
He's a worthless son of a bitch.

214
00:13:24,887 --> 00:13:26,514
He deserves to die.

215
00:13:29,976 --> 00:13:32,520
Stop! Fighting is bad!

216
00:13:40,528 --> 00:13:41,362
<i>Wait, what?</i>

217
00:13:44,782 --> 00:13:45,616
No way...

218
00:13:46,284 --> 00:13:48,453
Keiji's struggling?

219
00:13:48,911 --> 00:13:52,498
Is this really
the limit of your strength?

220
00:13:52,915 --> 00:13:54,000
Piece of—!

221
00:14:06,512 --> 00:14:10,266
<i>His movements are sloppy.
He's totally slow.</i>

222
00:14:15,021 --> 00:14:16,773
Let's call it, Brother.

223
00:14:16,939 --> 00:14:18,608
There's no use in continuing.

224
00:14:20,026 --> 00:14:21,110
Don't mess around.

225
00:14:21,819 --> 00:14:24,447
I'm not stopping until
I beat you to a pulp.

226
00:14:24,906 --> 00:14:28,117
Then I have no choice.
I'll put an end to this.

227
00:14:28,910 --> 00:14:29,744
Hatsu!

228
00:14:31,913 --> 00:14:32,747
Bou!

229
00:14:34,499 --> 00:14:35,333
Ten!

230
00:14:37,043 --> 00:14:37,877
Here I come...

231
00:14:42,131 --> 00:14:44,008
Turbulent Strike!

232
00:14:59,232 --> 00:15:01,025
H-He's...

233
00:15:02,235 --> 00:15:03,486
Ridiculously strong!

234
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:17,458
K-Kei...

235
00:15:22,130 --> 00:15:25,508
<i>To think my brother was this weak.</i>

236
00:15:26,676 --> 00:15:28,803
<i>Even if we teamed up,</i>

237
00:15:29,137 --> 00:15:30,805
<i>we wouldn't stand
a chance against them.</i>

238
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:35,268
<i>And now...
I've offended my brother.</i>

239
00:15:35,601 --> 00:15:36,435
Damn it!

240
00:15:36,561 --> 00:15:40,439
<i>Even now, Father's life
is in danger...</i>

241
00:15:41,190 --> 00:15:43,734
<i>I have no choice.
I can't give up!</i>

242
00:15:49,699 --> 00:15:51,409
<i>Of course, he's in shock...</i>

243
00:15:51,701 --> 00:15:54,287
<i>That must have been
the first time he's been beaten.</i>

244
00:15:58,833 --> 00:15:59,750
Piyoko?

245
00:16:01,502 --> 00:16:02,461
Mister!

246
00:16:03,254 --> 00:16:05,506
Eat this and feel better!

247
00:16:05,923 --> 00:16:06,757
Don't want it.

248
00:16:09,260 --> 00:16:11,304
Let's leave him alone right now.

249
00:16:14,098 --> 00:16:15,057
<i>Damn it...</i>

250
00:16:15,391 --> 00:16:18,561
<i>I couldn't keep up
with his last move at all.</i>

251
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:21,189
<i>Not to mention...
It felt like my body</i>

252
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:23,399
<i>was exploding from the inside...
It was unbelievable...</i>

253
00:16:24,192 --> 00:16:25,735
That bastard!

254
00:16:26,068 --> 00:16:28,905
I'll show him one day
by killing him!

255
00:16:30,573 --> 00:16:31,407
Big Brother...

256
00:16:32,658 --> 00:16:34,243
Bring it!

257
00:16:34,285 --> 00:16:36,037
This time, I'll beat you to a pulp!
Got it?

258
00:16:36,078 --> 00:16:37,538
That's not why I'm here!

259
00:16:39,457 --> 00:16:42,460
I'm sorry about earlier.
I was wrong.

260
00:16:43,127 --> 00:16:47,590
But I need to save our father,
no matter what!

261
00:16:48,466 --> 00:16:50,176
If Father dies...

262
00:16:50,301 --> 00:16:52,970
The world will fall into
the Demon's hands.

263
00:16:53,596 --> 00:16:55,681
He's someone who can't die yet.

264
00:16:56,474 --> 00:16:57,433
So please,

265
00:16:57,642 --> 00:16:59,560
help me save him!

266
00:16:59,894 --> 00:17:01,229
Please, Brother!

267
00:17:03,439 --> 00:17:04,857
Can I ask you a question?

268
00:17:05,816 --> 00:17:07,443
Miss E-Elizabeth!

269
00:17:07,777 --> 00:17:10,071
What you just said...
What does it mean?

270
00:17:10,821 --> 00:17:15,952
Well, Father and I have been
fighting to eradicate the Demons, too.

271
00:17:17,036 --> 00:17:18,287
Why?

272
00:17:18,537 --> 00:17:19,455
That's because...

273
00:17:20,373 --> 00:17:23,584
It's the duty of the Goshikidori Family.

274
00:17:25,253 --> 00:17:28,923
Our family and the Demons
have a long and intertwined history.

275
00:17:29,340 --> 00:17:31,801
We're the only ones
who can stop the Demons.

276
00:17:32,134 --> 00:17:35,054
<i>Family? Duty to stop the Demons?</i>

277
00:17:35,429 --> 00:17:37,098
<i>What is he talking about?</i>

278
00:17:37,723 --> 00:17:39,809
The same blood flows with you, Brother.

279
00:17:40,393 --> 00:17:44,188
That's why I need your help, please!

280
00:17:46,065 --> 00:17:48,359
Who cares.
It's got nothing to do with me.

281
00:17:48,776 --> 00:17:49,652
Brother...

282
00:17:51,821 --> 00:17:52,655
Hey...

283
00:17:53,239 --> 00:17:55,741
Can you tell us everything
that has happened?

284
00:17:56,450 --> 00:17:58,202
O-Of course.

285
00:18:00,204 --> 00:18:02,415
Even with your strength,
you couldn't defeat them?

286
00:18:02,790 --> 00:18:05,751
They must be plotting
something sinister

287
00:18:05,876 --> 00:18:08,170
with all of those Demons
that they're controlling.

288
00:18:08,879 --> 00:18:10,130
But to be honest,

289
00:18:10,131 --> 00:18:12,633
it might be difficult defeating
those Devils.

290
00:18:13,175 --> 00:18:14,260
But even so...

291
00:18:14,385 --> 00:18:16,512
I can't forsake our Father.

292
00:18:17,179 --> 00:18:20,766
I do not want to lose him.
No matter what.

293
00:18:23,477 --> 00:18:25,187
So, by the way...

294
00:18:25,313 --> 00:18:27,815
Do you know where
your father is being held?

295
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:32,612
Huh?! I-It's a warehouse
outside of town, in Akamori City.

296
00:18:32,945 --> 00:18:35,156
About 50 kilometers west from here.

297
00:18:35,865 --> 00:18:38,367
I-Is that one of those smartphones?

298
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:41,412
Oh, you know about them?
They're really handy!

299
00:18:42,455 --> 00:18:45,499
<i>M-Miss Elizabeth is so amazing!</i>

300
00:18:45,750 --> 00:18:49,503
Looks like there have been multiple
Demon sightings in Akamori City...

301
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:51,631
What?! Isn't this Demon...

302
00:18:51,839 --> 00:18:52,673
Keiji!

303
00:18:53,007 --> 00:18:56,427
Actually, I think we need to go
check this out ourselves.

304
00:18:59,388 --> 00:19:01,307
Mo... Morio...?!

305
00:19:02,808 --> 00:19:05,144
That kind Demon...

306
00:19:05,853 --> 00:19:08,606
<i>Why? Why is Morio...?</i>

307
00:19:12,985 --> 00:19:14,779
<i>What's gotten into you, Morio?</i>

308
00:19:18,908 --> 00:19:20,326
Did Morio do this?

309
00:19:20,451 --> 00:19:22,411
No way, Morio...

310
00:19:22,828 --> 00:19:24,664
According to the internet,

311
00:19:24,789 --> 00:19:28,334
Five Demons including Morio,
appeared all at once.

312
00:19:28,459 --> 00:19:30,920
An hour later,
they disappeared without a trace.

313
00:19:31,212 --> 00:19:33,631
Luckily,
no casualties were reported, but...

314
00:19:34,173 --> 00:19:37,385
It seems this town has been
the target of multiple Demon attacks.

315
00:19:37,635 --> 00:19:40,179
The abandoned factory
where the Devils are, is nearby.

316
00:19:40,596 --> 00:19:42,390
They've got to be behind this—!

317
00:19:45,309 --> 00:19:46,310
Demons!

318
00:19:46,811 --> 00:19:47,645
Let's go!

319
00:19:49,563 --> 00:19:51,649
<i>Is that you, Morio?</i>

320
00:19:55,111 --> 00:19:56,028
<i>Guess not.</i>

321
00:19:56,696 --> 00:19:59,490
I've fought this one
at the factory!

322
00:19:59,532 --> 00:20:00,365
What?!

323
00:20:00,366 --> 00:20:02,743
But I think
I've also seen this one before!

324
00:20:10,751 --> 00:20:11,919
There's no mistake!

325
00:20:12,336 --> 00:20:14,922
Stay back! He's mine!

326
00:20:15,047 --> 00:20:16,340
Don't order me around!

327
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:18,175
I fight by my own will alone!

328
00:20:20,553 --> 00:20:22,513
Stay down!

329
00:20:23,264 --> 00:20:24,098
Hatsu!

330
00:20:24,557 --> 00:20:25,391
Bou!

331
00:20:25,558 --> 00:20:26,726
Don't kill him!

332
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:29,937
That Demon used to be
one of the good ones!

333
00:20:30,146 --> 00:20:32,231
B-B-But!

334
00:20:32,356 --> 00:20:34,108
We can't just sit here
and do nothing!

335
00:20:34,316 --> 00:20:35,693
Leave this to me!

336
00:20:52,042 --> 00:20:54,670
It's made out of a special material,
so it shouldn't break.

337
00:20:56,338 --> 00:20:58,382
<i>She's so talented!</i>

338
00:21:07,683 --> 00:21:09,435
Hey! Spill it!

339
00:21:11,061 --> 00:21:13,397
Damn it, he's stubborn.

340
00:21:14,982 --> 00:21:19,445
We know the Goshikidori Family's
goal is to eliminate us.

341
00:21:19,904 --> 00:21:22,865
Was that silkie chicken
your only ally?

342
00:21:23,365 --> 00:21:25,868
I...have nothing to say to you.

343
00:21:26,076 --> 00:21:27,995
Damn it.
We'll see about that.

344
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:29,371
I-I have a report.

345
00:21:29,497 --> 00:21:30,331
Huh?

346
00:21:30,414 --> 00:21:31,916
What is it, Funakichi?

347
00:21:31,999 --> 00:21:33,542
You didn't forget to
have those Demons

348
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:35,085
let off some steam, did you?

349
00:21:35,211 --> 00:21:37,505
Y-Yes, about that...

350
00:21:37,838 --> 00:21:39,882
#56 has been defeated.

351
00:21:40,174 --> 00:21:41,675
Huh? By who?

352
00:21:41,884 --> 00:21:43,593
The chicken
who escaped the other day

353
00:21:43,594 --> 00:21:46,889
brought two others with him,
and they...

354
00:21:47,139 --> 00:21:48,516
I knew there were others.

355
00:21:49,475 --> 00:21:51,185
I bet they'll come here
sooner or later.

356
00:21:53,395 --> 00:21:54,271
Hey, Mama?

357
00:21:55,314 --> 00:21:58,400
If I catch those chickens,
will that make you proud?

358
00:22:01,946 --> 00:22:03,280
Yes, Hikari.

359
00:22:04,824 --> 00:22:06,992
That would make me very proud of you.

360
00:23:50,429 --> 00:23:52,681
Father! I'm coming to save you!

361
00:23:53,015 --> 00:23:54,558
Our opponents are countless Demons!

362
00:23:54,642 --> 00:23:56,101
I can't depend on
Big Brother at all!

363
00:23:56,185 --> 00:23:57,603
I have to give it my all,
or else—!

364
00:23:57,937 --> 00:24:00,855
Next episode: <i>Gone to the Birds</i>

365
00:24:00,856 --> 00:24:01,941
Miss Elizabeth?!

366
00:24:02,066 --> 00:24:04,026
You're too amazing!

367
00:24:04,818 --> 00:24:09,740
FAN ART CONTEST AWARDS

